Owned adapter, tests and qualification driver: S24 project.
GCM, inline block cipher and constant-time source/header files are unchanged
Mbed TLS 3.6.7, commit 068ff080b369adfac81509f9b57b2afabaf82dc5.
Copyright notices and SPDX declarations are preserved in each file. These
components are used under the upstream Apache-2.0 license option; the complete
license is src/platform/crypto/gcm/vendor/LICENSE. No Mbed TLS endorsement or
validation is implied.

The adapter imports the accepted src/platform/crypto/xts AES profile, AES source,
headers and sole mbedtls_platform_zeroize implementation read-only. Its common.h
has the previously accepted explicit freestanding include-only patch, whose
upstream and local hashes are verified against the complete official archive.
No GCM upstream primitive body is modified. New GCM/block-cipher/constant-time
entry symbols are namespaced via s24_gcm_profile.h; AES and zeroizer globals
remain owned by XTS. Any later provider must link the shared objects once.

The primary NIST GCM CAVP corpus is public test data from NIST. Running this
bounded subset is not CAVP, FIPS, Apple interoperability or side-channel validation.
Independent OpenSSL EVP execution uses the exact locally pinned shared library;
this does not claim that the library was reproduced from source by this task.
